  "body": "Sibling of the fix for Codex's other folders (phantom3792 on X: sessions and quota of accounts kept under another `CODEX_HOME`, such as `~/.codex-work`).\n\nRollouts, the usage ledger and the accounts now read every Codex folder (`appdir.CodexHomes`). Two readers still go by `CodexHome` alone:\n\n- **Thread names.** `codexTitleIndexPath()` in `internal/sessions/codex_titles.go` reads only `$CODEX_HOME/session_index.jsonl`. A session in another folder shows its first prompt, not the name the user gave it in Codex. The `codexTitles` cache holds one path, so reading several folders needs a cache for each path.\n- **State databases.** `codexStateDBs(home)` in `internal/sessions/codex_provider.go` honours `config.toml`'s `sqlite_home` only when `home == CodexDir()`. An extra folder that sets `sqlite_home` has its state DB looked for in the folder itself.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
