     "body": "Found while reviewing #3429. On origin/main b1f44d099, the sidebar's gateway line at the foot of the window keeps showing the old port after **Settings › Network › Gateway address › Apply** moves the gateway. It is corrected only by a reload or by something else that reads the providers again.\n\n## Reproduce\n\nI used the dev build in a sandbox HOME, with `port: 3483` in settings.json, no MAGPIE_ADDR and MAGPIE_DEV_UI=127.0.0.1:3484. Then, in Playwright (Chromium), I opened `?view=settings&tab=network`, typed 3486 and pressed Apply:\n\n```\nstart: Gateway 127.0.0.1:3483\nafter Apply: Gateway 127.0.0.1:3483 | settings says: ... Now http://127.0.0.1:3486\nafter reload: Gateway 127.0.0.1:3486\n```\n\nWith #3429's change (c28576084) the result is the same: 3481 → 3485, and the line still says 3481 until a reload.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe port save handler in app.js (`renderPort`'s `save.onclick`, the `settings/port` call) calls `renderSettings()` only. `sideGwAt` (the line's state) comes from the providers read, or now from boot.js, and nothing updates it after the move. `res.settings.gateway` already carries the new URL.\n\n## Why it isn't in the #3429 commit\n\napp.js is at its budget (TestCoreScriptBudget, 1,321,424 on main, with 25 bytes left after #3429). The fix (`renderSideGw` with `res.settings.gateway` after the save) needs room, which means moving something out of app.js first. Raising the budget is not the fix.\n",
